                  "type": "concept",
                  "title": "Five Eras of the Medical Record",
                  "content": "The modern HIM department is the product of **five distinct technology eras**. You cannot understand today's job descriptions without knowing the path that produced them.\n\n• **Paper era (pre-1970s)** — Standardized hospital records emerged after the **1918 ACS Hospital Standardization Program**. Records lived in folders, indexed on cards.\n\n• **Microfilm era (1960s–1980s)** — To save floor space, completed charts were photographed onto microfilm or microfiche. Retrieval still required a clerk and a reader machine.\n\n• **Early EMR era (1970s–1990s)** — Niche systems like **Lockheed's TMR**, **HELP at Intermountain**, and **VA's VistA** digitized parts of the chart for specific departments. Most hospitals were still 90 percent paper.\n\n• **EHR mandate era (2009–2015)** — The **HITECH Act of 2009** allocated roughly **$30 billion** in Medicare/Medicaid **Meaningful Use** incentives. Adoption of certified EHRs jumped from under 10 percent to over 96 percent of non-federal hospitals.\n\n• **Modern HIM era (2015–present)** — Data is digital and abundant. The job is now **governance, analytics, integrity, and protection** — not custody.",
                  "visual": {
                    "type": "diagram",
                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">FIVE ERAS OF THE RECORD</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Paper to data platform</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"180\" width=\"1000\" height=\"140\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"90\" y=\"230\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">1. PAPER  (pre-1970s)</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"270\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">ACS standardization, folders, index cards,</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"300\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">manual pulls — the chart was the original.</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"340\" width=\"1000\" height=\"140\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"90\" y=\"390\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">2. MICROFILM  (1960s–1980s)</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"430\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Photographed charts saved floor space</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"460\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">but retrieval still required a human.</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"500\" width=\"1000\" height=\"140\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(20,184,166,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"90\" y=\"550\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">3. EARLY EMR  (1970s–1990s)</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"590\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">TMR, HELP, VistA — niche, department-</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"620\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">specific systems beside paper charts.</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"660\" width=\"1000\" height=\"140\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"90\" y=\"710\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">4. EHR MANDATE  (2009–2015)</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"750\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">HITECH Act + Meaningful Use drove</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"780\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">adoption from under 10% to over 96%.</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"820\" width=\"1000\" height=\"140\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"90\" y=\"870\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">5. MODERN HIM  (2015–today)</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"910\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Govern, analyze, integrate, protect —</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"940\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">custody is replaced by stewardship.</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "The arc that produced the modern department"
                  }
