                {
                  "type": "concept",
                  "title": "Project Closing: The Ritual Most PMs Skip",
                  "content": "Most project managers race to the next thing the moment go-live happens. They skip **Closing** — and they keep making the same mistakes on the next project.\n\nClosing isn't ceremonial. It has **three critical rituals**:\n\n**1. Deliverable Handoff** — the project produced something (a new system, a workflow, a program). It must be **formally transitioned to operations**. Who owns it now? What's the SLA? Who supports it? **Document and sign the handoff** so there's no \"I thought you owned that.\"\n\n**2. Lessons Learned Meeting** — gather the team. Ask three questions:\n• What went well?\n• What went poorly?\n• What would we do differently next time?\n\nWrite it down. Store it in a shared location. **Read it before kicking off the NEXT project.** This is how organizations improve.\n\n**3. Stakeholder Thanks + Closure Communication** — send a closing email to the sponsor and stakeholders summarizing what was delivered, the benefits realized, and **thanking the team by name**. Project teams disband — but reputations carry forward. People remember who said thanks.\n\n**Bonus: PMP Certification** — the **Project Management Professional** credential from PMI is the gold standard. It requires 4,500-7,500 hours of project experience and a rigorous exam. **HIM leaders with PMP often command 15-25% salary premiums.**",
                  "visual": {
                    "type": "diagram",
                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">CLOSING THE PROJECT</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Three rituals most PMs skip</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"190\" width=\"1000\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"250\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">1. DELIVERABLE HANDOFF</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"300\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Formally transition to operations</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"340\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Document owner, SLA, support model</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"375\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">No more \"I thought you owned that\"</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"410\" width=\"1000\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"470\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">2. LESSONS LEARNED</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"520\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">What went well? What didn't?</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"560\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">What do we change next time?</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"595\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Read before kicking off the NEXT project</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"630\" width=\"1000\" height=\"200\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"690\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">3. THANKS + CLOSURE EMAIL</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"740\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Summarize delivery + benefits</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"780\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Thank team members BY NAME</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"815\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">People remember who said thanks</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"850\" width=\"900\" height=\"140\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"905\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">BONUS: PMP CERTIFICATION</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"950\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">PMI gold standard | 4,500-7,500 PM hours required</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"980\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">15-25% salary premium for HIM leaders</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"1010\" width=\"900\" height=\"70\" rx=\"35\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"1055\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Close it properly — or repeat your mistakes</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "Closing is where future projects get better"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "quiz",
                  "question": "On the project's RACI matrix, who can there be ONLY ONE of for each task or deliverable?",
                  "options": [
                    {
                      "text": "Responsible — the person doing the work",
                      "correct": false
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Accountable — the person who owns the outcome",
                      "correct": true
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Consulted — the subject matter expert",
                      "correct": false
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Informed — anyone needing status updates",
                      "correct": false
                    }
                  ],
                  "explanation": "On a RACI matrix, **Accountable** must be a single person per task — only one neck on the line for the outcome. You can have **multiple Responsible** workers, **multiple Consulted** experts, and **many Informed** stakeholders, but if more than one person is Accountable, nobody is truly accountable. This is why RACI matrices force teams to name a single owner for every deliverable.",
                  "visual": {
                    "type": "diagram",
                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">The RACI rule</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"190\" width=\"500\" height=\"180\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"250\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">R - RESPONSIBLE</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"300\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Does the work</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"340\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Can be multiple people</text><rect x=\"570\" y=\"190\" width=\"480\" height=\"180\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"810\" y=\"250\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">A - ACCOUNTABLE</text><text x=\"810\" y=\"300\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Owns the outcome</text><text x=\"810\" y=\"340\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">ONE PERSON ONLY</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"400\" width=\"500\" height=\"180\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"460\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">C - CONSULTED</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"510\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Gives input first</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"550\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Can be multiple SMEs</text><rect x=\"570\" y=\"400\" width=\"480\" height=\"180\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"810\" y=\"460\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">I - INFORMED</text><text x=\"810\" y=\"510\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Kept in the loop</text><text x=\"810\" y=\"550\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Can be many stakeholders</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"620\" width=\"900\" height=\"360\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"680\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">THE GOLDEN RULE</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"740\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">If more than one person is Accountable</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"780\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">then NOBODY is truly Accountable</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"840\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">One neck on the line</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"880\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">per task or deliverable</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"940\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">This is what makes RACI actually work</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"1010\" width=\"900\" height=\"70\" rx=\"35\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"1055\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">A = one person — always</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "Testing the RACI Accountable rule"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "quote",
                  "content": "Plans are nothing; planning is everything.",
                  "author": "Dwight D. Eisenhower",
                  "visual": {
                    "type": "diagram",
                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">WISDOM</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">From the man who planned D-Day</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"280\" width=\"940\" height=\"320\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"380\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-style=\"italic\" font-size=\"36\">\"Plans are nothing;</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"440\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-style=\"italic\" font-size=\"36\">planning is everything.\"</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"540\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-size=\"24\">— Dwight D. Eisenhower</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"680\" width=\"940\" height=\"280\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"740\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">WHY THIS MATTERS</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"800\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Your charter, WBS, and risk register</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"840\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">will be obsolete by week three</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"900\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">But the act of planning</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"940\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">prepares you to adapt</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"1010\" width=\"900\" height=\"70\" rx=\"35\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"1055\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Plan anyway — then change the plan</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "A moment of reflection from Eisenhower"
                  }
                }
